1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,759
AI can build a working app before its builder understands
the system.

2
00:00:05,759 --> 00:00:12,477
GroundTruth helps the learner understand code and
architecture, then practise the next change independently.

3
00:00:13,542 --> 00:00:16,268
Teachers face a connected problem.

4
00:00:16,268 --> 00:00:22,267
A polished, AI-assisted take-home artifact can conceal
gaps in independent understanding.

5
00:00:22,267 --> 00:00:28,266
Responsible AI learners also need a fair chance to
demonstrate ability.

6
00:00:28,266 --> 00:00:32,628
Reconstructing missing reasoning can add manual marking
work.

7
00:00:32,628 --> 00:00:38,627
This edited walkthrough uses real interface captures and
synthetic demo data.

8
00:00:39,708 --> 00:00:43,125
Start with a public repository and a feature.

9
00:00:43,125 --> 00:00:50,386
The learner chooses a backend workflow in our small
study-task app, before needing to know a filename.

10
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:55,608
The overview connects selected source to system
responsibilities.

11
00:00:55,608 --> 00:00:58,071
Where does a request go?

12
00:00:58,071 --> 00:01:00,042
Which component validates it?

13
00:01:00,042 --> 00:01:05,954
A reading flow and glossary help the learner build that
mental model.

14
00:01:07,208 --> 00:01:11,288
The concept tree links those responsibilities to focused
practice.

15
00:01:11,288 --> 00:01:19,901
It also gives teacher and learner a shared concept to
discuss, rather than relying only on the finished
artifact.

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,707
Muse Spark generates code-linked MCQs and tiny coding
tasks.

17
00:01:25,707 --> 00:01:29,891
The question responds to the source and goal.

18
00:01:29,891 --> 00:01:35,644
This is contextual practice, not AI grading of a take-home
project.

19
00:01:35,644 --> 00:01:38,782
Suggested answers still need source review.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,342
During an independent attempt, new study assistance
pauses.

21
00:01:44,342 --> 00:01:48,685
The original submitted response is preserved before
feedback.

22
00:01:48,685 --> 00:01:52,484
The learner may also end the attempt.

23
00:01:52,484 --> 00:01:56,827
GroundTruth cannot prevent outside help or infer
authorship.

24
00:01:58,083 --> 00:02:01,269
The learner chooses what to share.

25
00:02:01,269 --> 00:02:06,049
Original attempts and observed activity add context for
review.

26
00:02:06,049 --> 00:02:10,828
The concept index is provisional evidence, not a grade.

27
00:02:10,828 --> 00:02:14,545
These synthetic records are not learning-effectiveness
results.

28
00:02:15,667 --> 00:02:23,707
The teacher can inspect the original answer and identify a
concept worth a fresh unaided follow-up.

29
00:02:23,707 --> 00:02:27,728
This can inform teaching, while judgement stays human.

30
00:02:27,728 --> 00:02:33,758
Teacher AI quiz authoring, assignment distribution and
cohort analytics remain future work.

31
00:02:34,833 --> 00:02:37,376
Meta provides contextual content.

32
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:45,005
GroundTruth on Vercel controls access and learning state,
with Supabase preserving evidence.

33
00:02:45,005 --> 00:02:47,547
Support responsible AI learning.

34
00:02:47,547 --> 00:02:53,904
Understand the system, try independently, and make the
evidence inspectable.
